<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilgit-Baltistan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Northern Areas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gilgit-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltistan">Baltistan</a> is a territory administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in the north of the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> region, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. It came under Pakistani control after the 1947 uprising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and Kashmir, was long called the Northern Areas, and gained its present name and an elected assembly in 2009. It contains K2, Nanga Parbat and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakoram-highway">Karakoram Highway</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilgit-baltistan.jpg" alt="Gilgit-Baltistan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vasiq Eqbal · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trekkers_along_with_porters_towards_Snow_Lake,_over_Biafo_Glacier_61Km.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
